@marten-seemann It is impossible to rely on `largest_acked_packet_send_time`, because an ACK on another PN space might have arrived later than the persistent congestion period to be declared. See the example below.

![IMG_3331](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/41567/88139839-81b4ef00-cc2b-11ea-8c19-90abd434ed91.jpeg)

As stated in https://github.com/quicwg/base-drafts/pull/3889#discussion_r458524100, I do not think it is possible can use `loss_packets`, unless you implement some lossy behavior to bound state.

The following code makes sense to me at this moment:

```
   OnPacketsAcked(acked_packets):
     for (packet in acked_packets):
       // Remove from bytes_in_flight.
       bytes_in_flight -= packet.sent_bytes

     // Do not increase congestion_window if application
     // limited or flow control limited.
     if (IsAppOrFlowControlLimited())
       return

     for (packet in acked_packets):
       if (InCongestionRecovery(packet.time_sent)):
         // Do not increase congestion window in recovery period.
         continue
       if (congestion_window < ssthresh):
         // Slow start.
         congestion_window += packet.sent_bytes
       else:
         // Congestion avoidance.
         congestion_window += max_datagram_size * acked_packet.sent_bytes
           / congestion_window
```

